# React Aria UI primitives

`@eleva/ui` primitives are generated from the shadcn **`aria-luma`** style and built on
[`react-aria-components`](https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/react-aria/components.html).
Radix UI is **not** a dependency. See [ADR-022](../../docs/eleva-v3/adrs/ADR-022-react-aria-ui-primitives.md).

## Prop vocabulary (TypeScript enforces this)

| Radix / DOM habit          | React Aria                                   |
| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `disabled`                 | `isDisabled`                                 |
| `open` / `defaultOpen`     | `isOpen` / `defaultOpen`                     |
| `checked` / `onCheckedChange` | `isSelected` / `onChange`                 |
| `value` / `onValueChange` (Select) | `selectedKey` / `onSelectionChange`  |
| `onClick` (Button)         | `onPress`                                    |
| `onSelect` (MenuItem)      | `onAction` (or `href`)                       |
| `asChild`                  | render props, `href`, or `buttonVariants()`  |

`Select` and `Checkbox` participate in `<form>` natively via `name`; do not add hidden inputs.

## Composition rules

- **No `asChild`.** For links: `LinkButton` (client) or `<Link className={buttonVariants()}>` in Server Components. Any pressable (`Button`, `MenuItem`, `ListBoxItem`, `SidebarMenuButton`) accepts `href` directly.
- **Overlays are single components.** `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `AlertDialog`, `Popover`, `DropdownMenu` receive `isOpen` / `onOpenChange` and `className` themselves — do not nest a `*Content` wrapper unless the primitive still exports one.
- **`DropdownMenuTrigger` wraps trigger + menu**: `<DropdownMenuTrigger><Button/> <DropdownMenu>…</DropdownMenu></DropdownMenuTrigger>`. Items need `id` and `textValue` (typeahead + a11y).
- **`Checkbox` renders its own `<label>`.** Never wrap it in another `<label>`; use `CheckboxField` from `@eleva/ui/components/checkbox-field`.
- **Render props for hover/focus state**: `<SidebarMenuButton>{({ isHovered, isFocusVisible }) => …}</SidebarMenuButton>` instead of `group-hover` hacks where the state matters for icon swaps.
- **Tailwind state selectors**: `data-open`, `data-focused`, `data-selected`, `data-pressed`, `data-disabled` (custom variants from `shadcn/tailwind.css`). Do not write `data-[state=open]` — nothing emits `data-state` anymore.

## Routing

- `@eleva/dashboard` mounts `AppRouterProvider` (`@eleva/ui/components/router-provider`) so relative `href`s on React Aria components client-route via Next.js. Absolute URLs (`https://…`) fall through to a hard navigation for cross-zone links (ADR-014).
- `apps/web` intentionally does **not** mount it: marketing links must stay native anchors so gateway rewrites apply; use `next-intl`'s `Link` for locale-aware internal navigation.

## Regenerating primitives

```bash
cd packages/ui
pnpm exec shadcn add --overwrite <component>
```

Then fix imports: `cn` → `@eleva/ui/lib/utils`, icons → `@eleva/icons` (see `eleva-icons.mdc`).

**Local patches.** `--overwrite` discards every local change. Prefer extending by composition (`CheckboxField`, `SettingsFieldset`). When a registry bug or an Eleva a11y/product decision must live inside the primitive, mark it with an `// eleva:` comment explaining the divergence, and after regenerating run `rg -n "eleva:" packages/ui/src/components` against `git diff` to re-apply every patch. Current patches: `alert` (polite `status` role unless destructive), `card` (`CardTitle` renders `<h3>`, `as` override), `sidebar` (Cmd/Ctrl+B ignores editable targets; `showCloseButton={false}` on mobile; `SidebarMenu`/`SidebarMenuItem` stay `ul`/`li`), `sheet` (rest props go to the panel, not the overlay), `avatar` (fallback while loading, resync on `src` change, caller `onLoad`/`onError`/`ref` composed), `button` (`cursor-pointer`; `LinkButton` `data-disabled` styling), `checkbox` + `radio-group` (minus glyph for indeterminate; dead `data-checked` selectors removed), `command` (`data-selected`/`data-disabled` selectors; group heading styled directly instead of the cmdk attribute hook), `accordion` (`composeRenderProps` for render-prop `className`), `progress` (pulse while indeterminate), `select` (`SelectInput` `autoFocus` is a default, not forced; `SelectContent` placement `bottom start`), `dropdown-menu` (`defaultVariants.selectionMode`), `aspect-ratio` (caller `style` merged with `--ratio`), `dialog` + `sheet` + `alert-dialog` (`*Description` renders RAC `Text slot="description"` so `aria-describedby` is wired).

## Radix Themes

Do not add `@radix-ui/themes`. The previous widget peer is gone. Eleva UI is React Aria only. Plate may import other `@radix-ui/*` packages inside `packages/editor` (ADR-023), but never `@radix-ui/themes`.
